      "content": "Labor unions were essential in curbing corporate greed and protecting the public interest. They fought against companies that tried to bypass democratic norms to maximize profits. For example, in the 1930s, unions played a crucial role in the New Deal, pushing for legislation that regulated industries and protected workers' rights. They also fought against companies like Standard Oil, which was broken up in 1911 due to antitrust laws influenced by union activism. More recently, unions have fought against companies like Amazon and Walmart, advocating for better wages, benefits, and working conditions. These efforts have helped to ensure that corporations cannot exploit workers and the public at large. Labor unions have been a vital force in maintaining a fair and just society.",
